.\" Manpage for simple_shell.

.TH man 1 "05 September 2026" "1.0" "simple_shell man page"

.SH NAME
Holberton simple_shell
- A simple shell program coded in C with to interact with the linux operating system using already existing programs as well as remade ones

.SH SYNOPSIS

	./hsh
	$[executable] [arguments]

.SH DESCRIPTION

	Upon running the executable file for the simple_shell in interactive mode a banner will be printed to the terminal window as well as the prompt made up 
	of the CWD found in the environment followed by a '$'. 

	The program will attempt to run any command entered along with valid arguments by comparing against custom functions and searching for it in the $PATH.
	Where applicable it prints an error.It returns the status code of the last entered command which is always 0 if it was successful.

.SH OPTIONS

	All executables found in $PATH
	The following are the implemented custom commands:

		- setenv [name] [value] : sets or overwrites an environment variable given its name and value.
		- unsetenv [name] : removes an environment variable.
		- cd [name] : changes the current working directory and sets the previous working directory in the environment.
		- echo [string]: recreated in order to run it with variables like $?, $$ and $PATH. Limited argument options and functionality.
		- history : prints all commands entered that session


.SH SEE ALSO

	$PATH

.SH EXAMPLE

	BASH TERMINAL PROMPT$ ./hsh
	HOME/dir$ cd man
	HOME/dir/man$ cd -
	HOME/dir
	HOME/dir$ echo $?
	0

.SH BUGS

	If you attempt to cd with no parameters and OLDPWD is home, it will print the home directory.
	Handles a single '$' and '|' the same way a double occurence works.
	Pressing "Ctrl D" twice even when there is some text written to the promt will cause the shell to exit.


